---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
import CopyBlock from "../components/CopyBlock.astro";
import { packs, REPO_URL, href } from "../lib/site";

const example = `id: console-x
name: "Console X launch lures"
version: 1
as_of: 2026-11-21
keywords: [console-x, "console x"]
intents: [download, free, key, keygen, crack, apk, pc, beta, early-access, generator]
brands:
  - {name: examplestore, official: [example.com]}
allowlist:
  outlets: [example.org]
  platforms: []
facts:
  as_of: 2026-11-21
  facts:
    - id: pc_release
      claim: "No PC version announced (replace with a dated, sourced claim)."
      status: not_announced
      as_of: 2026-11-21
      sources: [{url: "https://example.com/source", title: "Source", accessed: 2026-11-21}]
  platforms:
    pc: {status: unreleased, fact: pc_release, terms: [pc, windows, steam]}`;
---
<Base title="Campaign packs: add a launch in 20 lines" description="LureRadar campaign packs describe one hyped launch in YAML: keywords, intents, brands, allowlist and dated facts. GTA 6 ships first; add your own launch in about 20 lines." og="packs">
  <PageHeader eyebrow="Campaign packs" title="One engine," em="many launches.">
    <p>LureRadar is a generic launch-lure engine. Everything campaign-specific lives in a pack: keywords, lure intents, brands that scammers impersonate (names only, never logos), legitimate outlets, and dated, sourced facts that drive rules such as “there is no PC version yet”.</p>
  </PageHeader>
  <div class="wrap">
    {packs.length ? packs.map((p) => (
      <article class="pack frame" data-reveal>
        <header class="pack-head">
          <p class="label-caps">Pack · <span class="mono">{p.id}</span> · v{p.version} · facts as of {p.as_of}</p>
          <h2>{p.name}</h2>
          <p class="pack-desc">{p.description}</p>
        </header>
        <div class="spec">
          <section>
            <h3 class="label-caps">Keywords</h3>
            <ul class="chips">{p.keywords.map((k: string) => <li>{k}</li>)}</ul>
          </section>
          <section>
            <h3 class="label-caps">Platforms</h3>
            <ul class="plat">{Object.entries(p.platforms).map(([, v]: [string, any]) => <li><span class={`lamp ${v.status === "unreleased" ? "amber" : ""}`} aria-hidden="true"></span><span>{v.label}</span><span class={`mono st ${v.status === "unreleased" ? "warn" : "okc"}`}>{v.status}</span></li>)}</ul>
          </section>
          <section>
            <h3 class="label-caps">Impersonated brands</h3>
            <ul class="brands">{p.brands.map((b: any) => <li><span>{b.name}</span><span class="mono muted">{b.official.join(" · ")}</span></li>)}</ul>
          </section>
          <section>
            <h3 class="label-caps">Allowlist</h3>
            <div class="allow">
              <div><span class="big">{p.allowlist_outlets}</span><span class="muted small">outlets, always CLEAR</span></div>
              <div><span class="big">{p.allowlist_platforms}</span><span class="muted small">user-content platforms, capped at SUSPICIOUS</span></div>
            </div>
          </section>
        </div>
        <section class="facts-wrap">
          <h3 class="label-caps">Facts on record</h3>
          <ol class="facts">{p.facts.map((f: any) => (
            <li>
              <div class="f-meta"><span class="mono">{f.id}</span><span class={`fstat fs-${f.status}`}>{String(f.status).replaceAll("_", " ")}</span><span class="mono muted">as of {f.as_of}</span></div>
              <p>{f.claim}</p>
              <p class="src">{f.sources.map((s: any, i: number) => <>{i ? " · " : ""}<a href={s.url}>{s.publisher ?? s.title ?? "source"}</a></>)}</p>
            </li>
          ))}</ol>
        </section>
      </article>
    )) : <div class="empty"><strong>No packs loaded</strong>Pack data appears after <code>build_site_data.py</code> runs.</div>}
    <h2>Add a launch in about 20 lines</h2>
    <p>Scaffold with <code>lureradar pack new console-x</code>, edit, then run <code>lureradar pack validate</code>. Every fact needs a date and a source. Full format in the <a href={href("docs/packs/")}>pack documentation</a>; propose one with the <a href={`${REPO_URL}/issues/new?template=new-campaign-pack.yml`}>new campaign pack</a> form.</p>
    <CopyBlock text={example} label="Copy example pack" />
  </div>
</Base>
<style>
  .pack { margin: 8px 0 72px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); background: var(--surface); }
  .pack-head { padding: clamp(22px, 3vw, 36px); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .pack-head h2 { margin: 10px 0 14px; font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4vw, 3.2rem); }
  .pack-desc { color: var(--text-2); max-width: 70ch; margin: 0; }
  .spec { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  .spec > section { margin: 0; padding: clamp(18px, 2.4vw, 28px); border-right: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .spec > section:last-child { border-right: 0; }
  .spec h3, .facts-wrap h3 { margin: 0 0 14px; }
  @media (max-width: 1000px) { .spec { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } .spec > section:nth-child(2) { border-right: 0; } .spec > section:nth-child(n + 3) { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); } }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .spec { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .spec > section { border-right: 0; } .spec > section + section { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); } }
  .chips { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px; }
  .chips li { font: 400 0.76rem/1 var(--font-mono); padding: 6px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border-strong); border-radius: 6px; color: var(--text-2); }
  .plat, .brands { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 10px; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .plat li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 14px 1fr auto; gap: 10px; align-items: center; }
  .plat .st { font-size: 0.72rem; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .brands li { display: grid; gap: 2px; }
  .brands .mono { font-size: 0.72rem; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .allow { display: grid; gap: 16px; }
  .allow > div { display: grid; gap: 4px; }
  .big { font: 650 3rem/0.9 var(--font-display); font-stretch: 66%; }
  .warn { color: var(--amber); }
  .okc { color: var(--radar); }
  .facts-wrap { margin: 0; padding: clamp(18px, 2.4vw, 28px); border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .facts { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .facts li { padding: 16px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .facts li p { margin: 8px 0 0; color: var(--text-2); max-width: 90ch; }
  .f-meta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 14px; align-items: center; font-size: 0.82rem; }
  .fstat { --c: var(--muted); font: 500 0.66rem/1 var(--font-mono); letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 4px 8px; border-radius: 999px; color: var(--c); border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--c) 40%, transparent); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--c) 9%, transparent); }
  .fs-confirmed { --c: var(--radar); }
  .fs-not_announced { --c: var(--amber); }
  .src { font-size: 0.82rem; }
  .src a { color: var(--muted); }
</style>
